- Downloaded from the registry into a fresh directory; SHA-1 and SHA-512 verified
  against those values. Tarball SHA-256 acbfae6890a122bae50adb520c8511a4f659c5bc45c577ae48d12424d730d745,
  10,009,266 bytes, 1,778 files. No npm pack from the working tree.

# Observed CI outcome on the released commit

CI run 39337367289 for the same commit is marked failure, but the router job log
shows "Ran 1366 tests ... OK" with no test failure. The exit code came from
tempfile.TemporaryDirectory.cleanup() raising
OSError: [Errno 39] Directory not empty: '/tmp/ciel-runtime-tests-rzssw__b'
while a child was still writing into the isolated test state. The other five jobs
passed. Recorded as a harness teardown race, not a product failure; it is not
changed by this release.

# Local install

- Before: HKCU CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME pointed at ~/.local/share/ciel-runtime-4e5c802900363fd318d1460b7510abd2ed08c24f
  and ciel-runtimectl reported 0.2.51-nightly.20261019-050605.4e5c802.
- npm global install of the exact version under C:/Users/djlov/AppData/Roaming/npm.
- install.ps1 run with CIEL_RUNTIME_INSTALL_HOME=~/.local/share/ciel-runtime-50e7906a1b4e3a104414adbbd40313de560a8c9c;
  the script registered that path in HKCU CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME.
- First attempt failed with npm ETARGET for the exact version while the registry
  packument already listed it; the retry with npm_config_prefer_online=true
  resolved it. The failed attempt created no snapshot and changed no registry value
  (checked).
- After: ciel-runtimectl reports 0.2.51-nightly.20261019-225158.50e7906; the
  launcher resolved from a non-repo working directory reports the same; the new
  snapshot holds 429 files; the previous 4e5c802 snapshot is untouched.

# Verification of the fix in the installed artifact

The installed snapshot's own code was executed (not the working tree):
window 872,000, percent 82, budget 716,750. Package and snapshot code trees are
byte-identical (recursive diff, no differences for ciel_runtime.py or
ciel_runtime_support). The DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 registration is present in the
installed providers/ollama.py.

Re-verification detail, including the client's effective-window arithmetic and a
61-provider sweep with zero violations, is in
docs/journal/2026/10/19/diagnostics/walkie-context-overflow/evidence/autocompact-trigger-client-semantics.txt.

# Limits

The running Claude Code session that produced this work was launched by the
4e5c802 runtime and keeps that code in its inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME until it is
restarted; it was not restarted. No live Claude or Codex launch was made after the
install to read the emitted environment from a child process. The packaged tarball
still ships 901 historical journal evidence files from earlier releases (pre-existing
behaviour, unchanged here); the private walkie-context-overflow evidence directory is
excluded by the root .npmignore and was confirmed absent from the tarball.
